AIGAMERIA Zero-Cost Open-Source and Free-Tier Technical Stack
Building AIGAMERIA on a 100% zero-cost, open-source, and free-tier-first stack requires splitting execution between client-side WebAssembly/JavaScript compute and quota-guarded Gemini API calls. Google publishes no official numerical quotas for its Gemini API free tier, and an independent API guide tracking two free-tier Google AI Studio projects as of November 11, 2026 measured limits of roughly 20 requests per day (RPD) for Flash and 500 RPD for 3.5 Flash-Lite, with Gemini 4 Carbon and Argon excluded from free-tier access entirely. Consequently, your React + Vite + Tailwind + Three.js application should offload continuous speech recognition, audio classification, and cryptographic proof validation to browser workers (Transformers.js, @contentauth/c2pa-web, and tlsn WASM) while reserving the Gemini Developer API and its free-tier Live API models (gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025 and 09-2025) for high-value coaching synthesis, multimodal frame review, and AI Court adjudication.
Across the Model Context Protocol (MCP) and GitHub ecosystems, active open-source tooling supports Chess.com, Lichess, Riot Games (League of Legends and Valorant), Steam, FACEIT CS2, Three.js/React Three Fiber, Blender, Supabase, Firebase, FFmpeg, VisionOS Glass UI, 3D Globes, VRM Avatars, and C2PA/zkTLS verification. Conversely, critical ecosystem gaps remain for Call of Duty and EA FC/FIFA live PvP match APIs (where kernel-level anti-cheat blocks injection and no verified open-source live-match MCP exists), browser anti-cheat telemetry and JS perceptual hashing (blockhash), and verified PandaScore/YouTube Data API free-tier quota schedules. Excluded from this stack are private or unreleased repositories (deven1003/chess-coach-mcp, Danyals-code/UI-Design-for-AVP), deprecated packages (c2pa legacy and c2pa-js-legacy), unmaintained 2022 wrappers (jakejrichards/cod-api), and paid proxy scrapers (trackergg-scraper).
1. Model Context Protocol Servers and Agent Skills
Antigravity and Gemini Workflow Skills
Inside Antigravity and the Gemini API managed agent (antigravity-preview-09-2026), SKILL.md packages load progressively—indexing only frontmatter metadata at session start—to prevent context bloat and irrelevant auto-activation. Installing Google's official gemini-skills pack is the highest-impact setup step: Google's self-reported evaluations on the repository indicate that adding these skills raised agent accuracy on Gemini API code generation to 87% with Gemini 3 Flash and 96% with Gemini 3.1 Pro. Furthermore, Antigravity's managed agent natively supports streamable HTTP MCP servers and cron-scheduled triggers with stored credentials, enabling automated background data syncs for clan wars or leaderboard updates.
