	Gaming Statistics, Match Histories, and Player Profiles
Cross-game telemetry divides cleanly between ecosystems with free public APIs (Chess.com, Lichess, Riot Games, Steam, and FACEIT) and closed publisher ecosystems (EA FC/FIFA and Call of Duty). For Chess and Riot titles, several 2025–2026 MCP servers support both local stdio for Antigravity and HTTP/SSE transports for web backends. Notably, prepaser/llm-chess-mcp exposes Stockfish, Leela Chess Zero (Lc0), and Maia3 (human-move likelihood conditioned on target Elo), letting AIGAMERIA distinguish objective calculation errors from human playstyle tendencies. For League of Legends, kostadindev/League-of-Legends-MCP exposes an SSE transport (--transport sse on port 8000) alongside Data Dragon static assets and an optional Gemini client.
For EA FC/FIFA and Call of Duty, no zero-cost official match-history API or full stats MCP exists in verified open-source registries. INSANE0777/Fc26-live-editor-mcp targets local EA FC 26 squad-file reverse engineering, while kupsas/football-data-mcp maps real-world SofaScore/xG soccer stats to EA FC attributes rather than player match logs. On the Call of Duty side, kernel anti-cheat blocks telemetry injection, prior API wrappers like jakejrichards/cod-api have been idle since 2022, and third-party scrapers rely on paid residential proxies. Consequently, AIGAMERIA should ingest EA FC and Call of Duty match results through user-submitted screenshots verified via the C2PA and zkTLS pipelines in Section 2.
