	Anti-Cheat and Proof of Skill
AIGAMERIA operates in a web browser and therefore cannot deploy kernel anti-cheat drivers; moreover, trying to hook native games guarded by Vanguard, VAC, or Call of Duty anti-cheat triggers immediate blocks. No standalone open-source browser anti-cheat telemetry library or JavaScript perceptual-hashing (blockhash) repository was confirmed in our ecosystem search. Instead, build AI Court and Proof of Skill around two verifiable cryptographic layers: C2PA Content Credentials (@contentauth/c2pa-web + ChronoVerify MCP) to authenticate captured gameplay screenshots/clips, and zkTLS / Zero-Knowledge Proofs (tlsnotary/tlsn, snarkjs) so players can prove stats fetched over HTTPS without exposing account credentials. Note that reclaimprotocol carries mixed licensing (MIT in .github/LICENSE versus a custom license in reclaimprotocol/tls and docs), so audit its terms before redistributing its TLS library.
